      "title": "Please Stop Telling Your AI to “Search Harder”",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O_qk3D3I3hI",
      "published_at": "2026-10-30T17:00:25+00:00",
      "author": "AAIF Live",
      "summary": "Humans used to give infrastructure a breather. AI agents don’t.\n\nIn this episode of Debug Mode, Erika and Demetrios explore what happens when one person’s prompt triggers a burst of searches, API calls, and compute-intensive requests - and why existing services, gateways, and pricing models can struggle to keep up.\n\nThey unpack the differences between microservices and agent workloads, revisit SaaS multi-tenancy, and explore Agent Substrate’s approach to actors, shared workers, sandboxes, and suspend-and-resume operations.\n\nAlong the way: cold starts, context persistence, a Spotify detour, and a practical question for anyone building with agents - do you actually need this infrastructure, or will it become another invisible layer inside the products you use?\n\nTimestamps:\n\n00:00 Agents put infrastructure under pressure\n02:10 Financial APIs meet agent traffic\n03:47 Why agent traffic is unpredictable\n08:13 API gateway pricing and surprise costs\n12:02 Microservices vs. agent workloads\n16:12 Context, identity, and multi-tenancy\n20:19 Restoring context and hiding latency\n22:07 Kubernetes and agent orchestration\n25:56 Agent Substrate: actors and workers\n28:23 Persistence, cold starts, and early limitations\n32:31 Spotify, prefetching, and musical twins\n36:54 Who actually needs this infrastructure?\n38:09 Do most agents need the cloud?\n42:33 Complexity, adoption, and hidden infrastructure\n43:57 Sandboxes and a next-episode teaser",
